1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,521
A roller coaster loops the loop.

2
00:00:02,521 --> 00:00:04,311
A toy car loops its track.

3
00:00:04,311 --> 00:00:06,869
A bucket of water swings over your head.

4
00:00:07,269 --> 00:00:09,586
All three go upside down at the top.

5
00:00:09,586 --> 00:00:11,235
So why does nothing fall?

6
00:00:11,685 --> 00:00:15,907
Aarav swings a bucket of water over
his head, in the college corridor.

7
00:00:16,257 --> 00:00:18,153
Fast, and not a drop falls.

8
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:19,765
Slow, and he gets wet.

9
00:00:19,765 --> 00:00:21,238
How slow is too slow?

10
00:00:21,738 --> 00:00:25,253
By the end, you will find that
speed with one short formula.

11
00:00:25,903 --> 00:00:28,485
So what is motion in a vertical circle?

12
00:00:28,835 --> 00:00:33,076
It is going round a circle that
stands up, like a wheel on the road.

13
00:00:33,476 --> 00:00:35,657
Going up, gravity slows the ball.

14
00:00:35,657 --> 00:00:37,653
Coming down, it speeds it up.

15
00:00:37,653 --> 00:00:39,454
So the speed keeps changing.

16
00:00:40,054 --> 00:00:41,180
Two forces act.

17
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,670
The string's pull, called tension, T.

18
00:00:43,670 --> 00:00:45,244
And the weight, m g.

19
00:00:45,644 --> 00:00:49,743
Their total pull toward the
centre must be m v squared over r.

20
00:00:49,743 --> 00:00:52,096
That bends the path into a circle.

21
00:00:52,746 --> 00:00:56,827
A half kilogram ball on a one
metre string, seen from the side.

22
00:00:57,177 --> 00:01:00,310
Start it at five metres
per second at the bottom.

23
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,877
It slows as it climbs.

24
00:01:02,277 --> 00:01:05,111
Just past the side, the tension hits zero.

25
00:01:05,111 --> 00:01:08,342
The string goes slack,
and the ball falls inside.

26
00:01:08,742 --> 00:01:11,148
Now start it at seven metres per second.

27
00:01:11,148 --> 00:01:13,060
It just makes it over the top.

28
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:17,528
On the graph, the pull is biggest at
the bottom, twenty nine point four

29
00:01:17,528 --> 00:01:19,421
newtons, and zero at the top.

30
00:01:19,921 --> 00:01:22,184
Slow-mo replay, at the very top.

31
00:01:22,534 --> 00:01:24,337
The string is not pulling.

32
00:01:24,337 --> 00:01:28,655
Gravity alone pulls the ball to
the centre, and it is just enough.

33
00:01:29,305 --> 00:01:32,227
Now let's find that speed, step by step.

34
00:01:32,577 --> 00:01:33,477
Step one.

35
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:37,660
At the top, T and m g both
point down, toward the centre.

36
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,679
So T plus m g equals m v squared over r.

37
00:01:41,429 --> 00:01:42,329
Step two.

38
00:01:42,218 --> 00:01:44,595
A string can pull, but never push.

39
00:01:44,595 --> 00:01:47,077
So the slowest case is T equals zero.

40
00:01:47,827 --> 00:01:48,804
Step three.

41
00:01:48,804 --> 00:01:51,501
Then m g equals m v squared over r.

42
00:01:51,501 --> 00:01:52,401
Cancel m.

43
00:01:52,372 --> 00:01:54,464
The top speed is root g r.

44
00:01:55,214 --> 00:01:56,126
Step four.

45
00:01:56,126 --> 00:01:57,026
Energy.

46
00:01:56,819 --> 00:01:59,525
From the top, the ball drops two r.

47
00:01:59,525 --> 00:02:03,218
So v bottom squared is v
top squared plus four g r.

48
00:02:03,218 --> 00:02:04,467
Root five g r.

49
00:02:05,217 --> 00:02:06,225
Remember this.

50
00:02:06,225 --> 00:02:09,787
On a string, the top speed
must be at least root g r.

51
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:13,511
Now, the bottom and the top, side by side.

52
00:02:13,861 --> 00:02:17,230
At the bottom, the weight
pulls away from the centre.

53
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:21,385
So the string holds the weight,
and gives m v squared over r too.

54
00:02:21,385 --> 00:02:22,395
T is biggest.

55
00:02:22,795 --> 00:02:26,180
At the top, the weight already
pulls toward the centre.

56
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,589
The string does less.

57
00:02:27,589 --> 00:02:28,623
T is smallest.

58
00:02:29,223 --> 00:02:30,215
Now you try.

59
00:02:30,215 --> 00:02:31,208
A weak rope.

60
00:02:31,208 --> 00:02:34,842
Where will it snap first,
at the bottom or at the top?

61
00:02:34,842 --> 00:02:36,076
Pause and decide.

62
00:02:39,276 --> 00:02:40,243
At the bottom!

63
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:43,546
There the rope holds the
weight, and also bends the path.

64
00:02:44,196 --> 00:02:48,259
Now swap the string for a
stiff rod, which can also push.

65
00:02:48,259 --> 00:02:51,255
On a rod, what is the slowest top speed?

66
00:02:51,255 --> 00:02:53,286
Root g r, or almost zero?

67
00:02:53,286 --> 00:02:54,613
Pause and decide.

68
00:02:57,813 --> 00:02:58,713
Almost zero!

69
00:02:58,709 --> 00:03:01,528
If the ball is slow, the rod pushes it up.

70
00:03:01,528 --> 00:03:03,487
It only has to reach the top.

71
00:03:04,137 --> 00:03:06,108
So why does Aarav's water stay in?

72
00:03:06,108 --> 00:03:07,195
Follow the links.

73
00:03:07,545 --> 00:03:08,445
One.

74
00:03:08,097 --> 00:03:13,180
At the top, the water needs a pull
of m v squared over r, downward.

75
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:14,480
Two.

76
00:03:14,013 --> 00:03:15,888
Its weight, m g, gives some.

77
00:03:15,888 --> 00:03:18,468
The bucket base pushes
down to give the rest.

78
00:03:18,868 --> 00:03:19,768
Three.

79
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:22,962
Swung fast, m v squared
over r is more than m g.

80
00:03:22,962 --> 00:03:25,641
The base presses, and the water stays.

81
00:03:26,041 --> 00:03:26,941
Four.

82
00:03:26,562 --> 00:03:29,103
Swung slowly, m g is more than needed.

83
00:03:29,103 --> 00:03:31,736
Gravity pulls the water out of the circle.

84
00:03:31,736 --> 00:03:32,695
He gets wet.

85
00:03:33,295 --> 00:03:34,985
Now, one worked example.

86
00:03:35,335 --> 00:03:39,721
Aarav's bucket holds one kilogram
of water, on a circle of radius zero

87
00:03:39,721 --> 00:03:41,053
point nine metres.

88
00:03:41,553 --> 00:03:43,910
The slowest top speed is root g r.

89
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:46,956
Root of nine point eight
times zero point nine.

90
00:03:46,956 --> 00:03:48,945
About three metres per second.

91
00:03:49,695 --> 00:03:52,386
At the bottom, v squared is five g r.

92
00:03:52,386 --> 00:03:54,409
That is forty four point one.

93
00:03:55,159 --> 00:03:58,761
So the base pushes up with
m g plus m v squared over r.

94
00:03:58,761 --> 00:04:00,881
Nine point eight plus forty nine.

95
00:04:00,881 --> 00:04:02,898
Fifty eight point eight newtons.

96
00:04:03,648 --> 00:04:05,304
Six times the water's weight.

97
00:04:05,304 --> 00:04:07,190
His arm feels it at the bottom.

98
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,302
Now, the exam trap.

99
00:04:09,652 --> 00:04:14,851
Many students write the top equation
as T equals m v squared over r, plus

100
00:04:14,851 --> 00:04:15,751
m g.

101
00:04:15,831 --> 00:04:19,786
But at the top, gravity
points toward the centre too.

102
00:04:19,786 --> 00:04:23,202
So T equals m v squared over r, minus m g.

103
00:04:23,852 --> 00:04:25,144
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:25,144 --> 00:04:29,028
In numericals on top and bottom
speeds, and the tension at a point.

105
00:04:29,628 --> 00:04:30,785
Exam level now.

106
00:04:30,785 --> 00:04:35,638
A point two kilogram ball whirls in a
vertical circle on a one metre string.

107
00:04:35,638 --> 00:04:38,873
The top tension is three
newtons, and g is ten.

108
00:04:38,873 --> 00:04:40,529
Find the bottom tension.

109
00:04:40,529 --> 00:04:41,735
Pause and solve.

110
00:04:47,135 --> 00:04:48,422
The answer is C.

111
00:04:48,422 --> 00:04:49,590
Fifteen newtons.

112
00:04:50,090 --> 00:04:53,624
At the top, T plus m g
is m v squared over r.

113
00:04:53,624 --> 00:04:57,670
Three plus two is five, so v
top squared is twenty five.

114
00:04:58,170 --> 00:04:59,070
Energy.

115
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:04,236
Down two metres, v bottom squared is
twenty five plus forty, sixty five.

116
00:05:04,736 --> 00:05:08,181
At the bottom, T is m g
plus m v squared over r.

117
00:05:08,181 --> 00:05:09,479
Two plus thirteen.

118
00:05:09,479 --> 00:05:10,621
Fifteen newtons.

119
00:05:11,221 --> 00:05:12,761
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:12,761 --> 00:05:14,343
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:17,543 --> 00:05:19,730
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

122
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:21,030
One.

123
00:05:20,577 --> 00:05:23,336
Why does the speed change
on a vertical circle?

124
00:05:24,236 --> 00:05:25,136
Two.

125
00:05:24,645 --> 00:05:27,219
Why can the top speed
on a string not be zero?

126
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,019
Three.

127
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:31,464
Where does the string
pull hardest, and why?

128
00:05:32,564 --> 00:05:36,385
Next time: two friends climb
the same stairs, one faster.

129
00:05:36,385 --> 00:05:37,796
Who has more power?

130
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:39,364
We find out in power.
